# Walk-through of the service, one request per endpoint, run against the local demo (see "Run it" in the README):
# the fake Graph server on :5103 and the API on :5102, both with the Development settings.
# Syntax: VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP client. Run the requests top to bottom.
# Each request states the status code it returns when the walk-through is followed in order, and where to wait
# for the dispatcher, the fake's webhooks or the reconciler first.
#
# A webhook signature (X-Hub-Signature-256) cannot be written by hand, so every SIGNED webhook in this file is
# posted by the fake Graph server: inbound messages through POST {{graph}}/_inspect/inbound, status receipts
# automatically after each message it accepts. The only hand-written webhook calls are the handshake and a
# deliberately unsigned delivery.
#
# The keys and secrets below are the demo values of appsettings.Development.json. They are not secrets.

@api = http://localhost:5102
@graph = http://localhost:5103
@tenantKey = dev-only-tenant-a-key-not-a-secret
@adminKey = dev-only-admin-key-not-a-secret
@expiredTenantKey = dev-only-tenant-expired-key-not-a-secret
@disabledTenantKey = dev-only-tenant-disabled-key-not-a-secret
@verifyToken = dev-only-verify-token-not-a-secret
@phoneNumberId = 100200300
@recipient = +12025550100
@otherRecipient = +12025550143

### 1. Liveness. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/health/live

### 2. Readiness: checks the database and the dispatcher. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/health/ready

### 3. The OpenAPI contract, behind the same API key. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/openapi/v1.json
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 4. Start clean: forget what the fake Graph server received and posted. Expect: 204
DELETE {{graph}}/_inspect/messages

### 5. Remove failure rules left over from an earlier run. Expect: 204
DELETE {{graph}}/_inspect/failures

### 6. Remove outcome rules left over from an earlier run. Expect: 204
DELETE {{graph}}/_inspect/outcomes

### 7. A booking is created. The event is queued, never sent inline. Expect: 202
POST {{api}}/api/v1/events/booking-created
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-booking-created
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "bk-1001",
  "reference": "REF-1001",
  "customerFirstName": "Sam",
  "phoneCountryCallingCode": "1",
  "phoneNationalNumber": "2025550100",
  "bookingType": "Hotel",
  "status": "Confirmed",
  "details": { "checkInDate": "2026-03-14" },
  "companyName": "Acme Travel",
  "createdAt": "2026-03-01T09:30:00Z",
  "preferredLanguage": "en",
  "whatsappUpdatesEnabled": true
}

### 8. Give the dispatcher a moment (wait 2 seconds), then look at what the fake Graph server received. Expect: 200 (one template message)
GET {{graph}}/_inspect/messages

### 9. The same event again. Expect: 202 (accepted, but nothing new is queued)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/events/booking-created
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "bk-1001",
  "reference": "REF-1001",
  "customerFirstName": "Sam",
  "phoneCountryCallingCode": "1",
  "phoneNationalNumber": "2025550100",
  "bookingType": "Hotel",
  "status": "Confirmed",
  "details": { "checkInDate": "2026-03-14" },
  "companyName": "Acme Travel",
  "createdAt": "2026-03-01T09:30:00Z",
  "preferredLanguage": "en",
  "whatsappUpdatesEnabled": true
}

### 10. Still exactly one message at the fake Graph server. Expect: 200
GET {{graph}}/_inspect/messages

### 11. Delivery receipts: the fake posted signed sent, delivered and read webhooks. Filter by delivery status (wait 4 seconds). Expect: 200
# @name readList
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications?deliveryStatus=Read
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 12. One notification with its receipt timeline and derived delivery status. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{readList.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}

### 13. A status change. Expect: 202
POST {{api}}/api/v1/events/booking-status-changed
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "bk-1001",
  "reference": "REF-1001",
  "customerFirstName": "Sam",
  "phoneCountryCallingCode": "1",
  "phoneNationalNumber": "2025550100",
  "bookingType": "Hotel",
  "status": "ConfirmedPendingPayment",
  "details": { "checkInDate": "2026-03-14" },
  "companyName": "Acme Travel",
  "createdAt": "2026-03-01T09:30:00Z",
  "preferredLanguage": "ar",
  "whatsappUpdatesEnabled": true
}

### 14. A custom free-text notification. No inbound message yet, so the 24 hour window is closed. Expect: 202
# @name freeTextClosed
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{otherRecipient}}",
  "kind": "FreeText",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-1",
  "text": "Hi, your order is ready for pickup."
}

### 15. The same request again. Expect: 200 (duplicate: true, same id)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{otherRecipient}}",
  "kind": "FreeText",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-1",
  "text": "Hi, your order is ready for pickup."
}

### 16. Read it back (wait 2 seconds): Skipped with the reason "window closed". Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{freeTextClosed.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}

### 17. A customer writes to the business number. The fake posts a SIGNED inbound webhook to the service, which opens the 24 hour window through the real webhook path. Expect: 200
POST {{graph}}/_inspect/inbound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from": "{{recipient}}",
  "phoneNumberId": "{{phoneNumberId}}",
  "text": "Hello, is my booking confirmed?"
}

### 18. DEMO ONLY: the admin shortcut feeds the same recorder as the webhook, so it has the same effect. Expect: 200
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/conversations/inbound
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "tenant-a",
  "recipient": "{{recipient}}"
}

### 19. Free text is now allowed. Expect: 202
# @name freeTextOpen
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{recipient}}",
  "kind": "FreeText",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-2",
  "textVariants": {
    "en": "Hi {name}, your order is ready for pickup.",
    "ar": "مرحباً {name}، طلبك جاهز للاستلام."
  },
  "placeholders": { "name": "Sam" },
  "preferredLanguage": "en"
}

### 20. Delivered as text this time (wait 2 seconds). Expect: 200
GET {{graph}}/_inspect/messages?to=%2B12025550100

### 21. Free text with a template fallback: sent as a template when the window is closed. Expect: 202
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{otherRecipient}}",
  "kind": "FreeText",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-3",
  "text": "Your booking is confirmed.",
  "template": {
    "name": "booking_status_updated",
    "parameters": ["Sam", "REF-1001", "Confirmed"]
  }
}

### 22. The webhook handshake: the verify token matches, so the challenge is echoed as plain text. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/webhooks/whatsapp?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.verify_token={{verifyToken}}&hub.challenge=1158201444

### 23. The handshake with a wrong token. Expect: 403
GET {{api}}/api/v1/webhooks/whatsapp?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.verify_token=not-the-token&hub.challenge=1158201444

### 24. A delivery without a valid signature is turned away before anything is read from it. Expect: 401
POST {{api}}/api/v1/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "object": "whatsapp_business_account", "entry": [] }

### 25. What the fake posted to the webhook, and how the service answered. Expect: 200
GET {{graph}}/_inspect/webhooks

### 26. Failure injection: the next request to the fake Graph server is rejected as an invalid recipient. Expect: 201
POST {{graph}}/_inspect/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "invalid-recipient", "remaining": 1, "recipient": "{{recipient}}" }

### 27. A template notification that will hit the injected failure. Expect: 202
# @name doomed
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{recipient}}",
  "kind": "Template",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-4",
  "template": {
    "name": "booking_status_updated",
    "languageCode": "en",
    "parameters": ["Sam", "REF-1001", "Cancelled"]
  }
}

### 28. Permanent error (wait 2 seconds): the row is dead-lettered, not retried. Expect: 200 (status DeadLettered)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{doomed.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 29. An admin retries it. Expect: 202
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{doomed.response.body.$.id}}/retry
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 30. This time it goes through (wait 2 seconds). Expect: 200 (status Sent)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{doomed.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 31. Retrying something that is not failed is refused (it is Sent). Expect: 409
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{doomed.response.body.$.id}}/retry
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 32. A tenant whose token has expired: permanent error with its own kind. Expect: 202
# @name expired
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{expiredTenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{recipient}}",
  "kind": "Template",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-5",
  "template": {
    "name": "booking_status_updated",
    "languageCode": "en",
    "parameters": ["Sam", "REF-1001", "Confirmed"]
  }
}

### 33. DeadLettered with a TokenExpired error (wait 2 seconds). Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{expired.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 34. A disabled tenant is skipped, not failed. Expect: 202
POST {{api}}/api/v1/events/booking-created
X-Api-Key: {{disabledTenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "bk-2001",
  "reference": "REF-2001",
  "customerFirstName": "Alex",
  "phoneCountryCallingCode": "1",
  "phoneNationalNumber": "(212) 555-0143",
  "bookingType": "Flight",
  "status": "Confirmed",
  "details": {
    "departureAt": "2026-04-02T08:30:00Z",
    "origin": "AAA",
    "destination": "BBB"
  },
  "companyName": "Acme Travel",
  "createdAt": "2026-03-01T09:30:00Z",
  "whatsappUpdatesEnabled": true
}

### 35. A failed receipt: the fake reports the next message to this number as undeliverable. Expect: 201
POST {{graph}}/_inspect/outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "recipient": "{{recipient}}", "final": "failed", "errorCode": 131026, "errorTitle": "Message undeliverable", "remaining": 1 }

### 36. A template notification to that number. Expect: 202
# @name undeliverable
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{recipient}}",
  "kind": "Template",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-6",
  "template": {
    "name": "booking_status_updated",
    "languageCode": "en",
    "parameters": ["Sam", "REF-1001", "Confirmed"]
  }
}

### 37. The provider accepted it and then reported a failure (wait 5 seconds): Failed, with the reason, and not sent again. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{undeliverable.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}

### 38. Crash after accept: the next message to this number is accepted by the fake, but the connection drops before the answer. Expect: 201
POST {{graph}}/_inspect/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "drop-after-accept", "remaining": 1, "recipient": "{{otherRecipient}}" }

### 39. ... and the fake sends no receipts for it. Expect: 201
POST {{graph}}/_inspect/outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "recipient": "{{otherRecipient}}", "final": "none", "remaining": 1 }

### 40. A template notification to that number. Expect: 202
# @name dropped
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "{{otherRecipient}}",
  "kind": "Template",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-7",
  "template": {
    "name": "booking_status_updated",
    "languageCode": "en",
    "parameters": ["Sam", "REF-1001", "Confirmed"]
  }
}

### 41. The service cannot know whether the message was sent (wait 3 seconds): Unconfirmed, and it is not sent again. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{dropped.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 42. After the grace period (15 seconds in the Development settings) with no receipt, the default policy dead-letters it for a human to decide (wait 17 seconds). Expect: 200 (status DeadLettered, error starts with "unconfirmed")
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{dropped.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 43. An admin retries it. Expect: 202
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{dropped.response.body.$.id}}/retry
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 44. Sent this time (wait 2 seconds). Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/{{dropped.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 45. All notifications, newest first (admin). Filter with status, recipient, tenantId, deliveryStatus, page, pageSize. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications?pageSize=50
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 46. Only the skipped ones. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications?status=Skipped
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 47. Only the ones the provider reported as failed. Expect: 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications?deliveryStatus=Failed
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 48. A tenant key cannot use admin routes. Expect: 403
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}

### 49. No key at all. Expect: 401
GET {{api}}/api/v1/notifications/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 50. Validation errors are RFC 7807 problem documents. Expect: 400
POST {{api}}/api/v1/notifications
X-Api-Key: {{tenantKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipient": "12",
  "kind": "Template",
  "eventKey": "order-update",
  "referenceKey": "order-8",
  "template": { "name": "booking_status_updated", "parameters": ["only one"] }
}
